## Phase 7 — Complete the other launch surfaces

The staff tablet is the largest missing track, but it is not the entire product.

### 23. Polish the rider mobile MVP

The mobile shell already exists. Focus additions on:

- Lamphun station and return-zone data.
- Final PDPA and identity flow.
- Local/tourist registration.
- Bike-status blocker explanations.
- Approved payment/reference flow.
- Station-based return guidance.
- Bilingual rider-facing copy.
- Emergency and station-support paths.
- Clear simulated/app-assisted unlock messaging until physical lock integration is confirmed.

### 24. Extend the admin operations web app

Beyond tablet conflict review, add or complete:

- Staff and role management.
- Station operations.
- Payments/reconciliation.
- Incidents.
- Maintenance/work orders/QC.
- Manual battery logs.
- Daily/monthly reports.
- Government read-only mode.
- Estimated versus verified metric labels.

Maintenance is launch-critical because failed inspections must lead to an actionable repair and QC workflow.

### 25. Define reports and exports

Required daily outputs include:

- Rentals and returns.
- Active/unreturned rentals.
- Fleet availability.
- Blocked bikes.
- Revenue/payment reconciliation.
- Incidents/damage.
- Maintenance activity.
- Battery exceptions.
- Backup-mode activations.
- Manual overrides.
- Data-completeness exceptions.

Monthly/government reporting adds:

- Station utilization.
- Availability rate.
- Repair SLA and PM compliance.
- Revenue and exceptions.
- Complaints/satisfaction.
- Estimated carbon reduction.
- Audit summary.

The exact Lamphun PAO report requirements and carbon formula remain unresolved.

